VSaAAVERjMZ6KvWBG2Yupcm\",\"/mintlify-assets/_next/static/chunks/0eb894a8519f24ea.js?dpl=dpl_HYbBsVSaAAVERjMZ6KvWBG2Yupcm\",\"/mintlify-assets/_next/static/chunks/c059c9cd8bff0e61.js?dpl=dpl_HYbBsVSaAAVERjMZ6KvWBG2Yupcm\",\"/mintlify-assets/_next/static/chunks/68d6e5104243ae2b.js?dpl=dpl_HYbBsVSaAAVERjMZ6KvWBG2Yupcm\",\"/mintlify-assets/_next/static/chunks/6a8e2fc12e413a1c.js?dpl=dpl_HYbBsVSaAAVERjMZ6KvWBG2Yupcm\",\"/mintlify-assets/_next/static/chunks/d3838a955978f85b.js?dpl=dpl_HYbBsVSaAAVERjMZ6KvWBG2Yupcm\",\"/mintlify-assets/_next/static/chunks/65712ea96ab292b5.js?dpl=dpl_HYbBsVSaAAVERjMZ6KvWBG2Yupcm\",\"/mintlify-assets/_next/static/chunks/84e0cf38487df0b6.js?dpl=dpl_HYbBsVSaAAVERjMZ6KvWBG2Yupcm\"],\"ScopedNavProvider\"]\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"48:T5f1,"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"How fresh the data behind this API is.\n\n`/readyz` answers whether this pod can reach its datastore; this answers how\nfar behind chain head what you are reading is. Two halves, because each is\nblind exactly where the other sees:\n\n* `serving`; the projections that turn ingested rows into what the feeds\n  read (`activity_feed` enrichment, `custody_balances` ingestion, the PnL\n  engine).\n  Each carries its own clock, so this is the only half that can see\n  \"everything stopped\". `lag_seconds` is the worst age across them and\n  `worst` names which one, so a single stalled projection cannot hide behind\n  two healthy ones.\n* `ingestion`; one crawl cursor per `(contract, event)`, summarised as the\n  tail, the furthest-behind block, and the worst few cursors BY NAME. Every\n  reading here is relative or positional, so under a total stall it reads\n  green; that is why `serving` exists alongside it.\n\nStreams that are dormant by design are dropped from `ingestion` rather than\nreported, because they sit arbitrarily far back forever and would otherwise\nfill the list and push the stream you care about off it.\n\nTakes no parameters and is not paginated. Served from a snapshot refreshed\nin the background, never computed on the request: `computed_at` and\n`age_seconds` say how old it is, so a stalled refresher or a datastore\noutage shows up as a growing age rather than a 500. Before the first refresh\nlands there is nothing to serve and this answers `503`; \"not measured yet\"\nand \"measured, no lag\" are different claims."])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"49:T4b4,"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"Top holders of a market, netted per user and grouped by\noutcome token.\n\n`?condition=` (CSV of `condition_id`) is required (400 otherwise). `?limit=`\n(default 100, max 1000; v2 family-uniform) sizes the page **per outcome\ntoken**; `?min_balance=` filters the served amount.\n\n`?include_pnl=true` opts each holder row into the position economics\n(entry price and cost, current price and value, realized, unrealized and\ntotal profit) and switches the amounts to per-side gross balances, so a\nwallet holding both outcomes appears under both tokens. The default\nresponse is unchanged. This mode serves one market's table at a time:\nexactly one `condition` and `limit` at most 100 (400 otherwise, including\nvia a cursor that carries a wider window).\n\nA malformed condition id is a `400` naming the value; a well-formed one\nthat resolves to no holdings serves an empty `data` array, which is the\nmeaningful zero-state.\n\nDeeper pages come only from `?cursor=` (which carries the page window and\noverrides `limit`).\n\nPage walks advance every token group together, so a group leaves `data`\nonce its token is exhausted while others keep paging; no rows are lost,\nbut merge pages by `token_id`, not by array position."])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"4a:Tbec,"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"The price-history series for one outcome token, or\na single point-in-time observation.\n\nThree window forms, exactly one per request: `start` (with optional `end`),\n`interval`, or `as_of`. Points are served oldest-first; pass `?cursor=` from\na prior response's `next_cursor` for the next page.\n\n`interval=max` (or `all`) serves the market's whole life, back to 2022 for\nthe oldest markets, at 12-hour buckets unless `bucket_seconds` says\notherwise; explicit `start`/`end` windows cap at 15 days, so the presets\nare the long-range path.\n\nThe series ends with a **terminal point**: the latest observation inside the\nwindow, which is a real tick and so can fall between bucket boundaries.\nNothing may assume uniform spacing (sparse data already forbids that), and\neach point's `resolution_seconds` says what window it was observed in.\n\n**Availability is graded by resolution.** The 3-hour and 12-hour series are\npermanent (back to 2022-11-18); the fine grains are windowed, with these\nMINIMUMS: 1-minute data at least 7 days, 5-minute at least 60, 30-minute at\nleast 90. Floors, not exact horizons: data expires in multi-day chunks, so a\ngrain usually reaches a few days further back than its minimum. Coverage is\nmeasured per request, never assumed from a table, so `bucket_seconds=60`\nover a window starting a month ago is an incompatible pair: both values are\nvalid, and there is no data at their intersection.\n\nThe two ways of asking behave differently on purpose:\n\n* **`bucket_seconds` sent** is served exactly as asked, so over a window\n  whose resolution has expired you get an empty page rather than a silent\n  substitution.\n* **`bucket_seconds` omitted** lets the server choose a width that can\n  actually serve the window: the finest tier grain whose series stays under\n  ~2,500 points, except that a window wider than 12 hours never defaults to\n  the 60-second grain (ask for `bucket_seconds=60` explicitly when you want\n  it over a longer window), and\n  coarsened further if that grain does not reach the window's start. A\n  window up to 12 hours keeps 1-minute detail (an hour 60 points, 12 hours\n  720); beyond that it moves to a materialized tier (a day 288, three days\n  864, a week 2,016, fifteen days 720). Send `bucket_seconds` when you want\n  a specific density instead.\n\nA RESOLVED market's series ends with one settlement point: the on-chain\npayout of the requested token (0 lost, 1 won, fractional for voided or\nsplit resolutions) at `resolution_seconds` 0, placed one bucket edge past\nthe last stored row and clamped to an explicit window's `end`. It appears\nonly on the final page of a paginated walk, and only once the resolution\nis settled on-chain; an unresolved market's series is unchanged.\n\n`resolution_seconds` on every point reports what it was served at, so read it\ninstead of assuming the width a recent window would have given you. For a\nmulti-day window prefer a grain-aligned `bucket_seconds` (300, 1800, 10800,\n43200) or omit it; a 60-second width over days is the one shape that is both\nslow and, past 7 days, empty."])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"4b:T523,"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"The profile card for one wallet in a single call.\n\n`?user=` is required. Returns `{ data: { trades, biggest_win, views,\njoin_date, all_time_pnl } }`, or `{ data: null }` when the wallet is not a\nknown user.\n\n**`data: null` and a row of zeros mean different things.** `null` is \"no such\nuser\"; zeros are \"this user exists but has never traded, never won and has no\nprofile views\".\n\n`trades` counts DISTINCT MARKETS traded, not individual trades. It is exact,\nnot estimated.\n\n`biggest_win` is the best single **resolved** position win in USDC, market\nand combo arms unified, and `0` when the wallet has no win over $1.\n\n`join_date` is epoch seconds, or `null` when unknown.\n\n`all_time_pnl` is the newest persisted cumulative `/v2/user-pnl` point at\nits actual observation timestamp. It is `null` when the user exists but no\nobservation has been published yet. For the composition card: trading\nrealized is `realized_market_pnl + realized_combo_pnl`; LP realized is\n`realized_lp_pnl`; rebates, yield, rewards, referral, and fees paid map to\ntheir same-named fields (`fees_paid` is refunds minus charges). `volume`,\n`volume_usdc`, and `trade_count` are cumulative maker-attributed canonical\nfill metrics.\n\nNot paginated: one row by construction, so `data` is the bare object with no\n`pagination`; the `/v2/value` shape."])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"4c:T595,"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"A keyset page of positions in the standard\n`{ data, pagination }` envelope. One route serves a user's open book, their\nclosed book (`status=CLOSED`), and a market's holders (market anchor).\n\nAt least one of `user`/`condition` is required. Supplying both anchors on the\nuser and applies `condition` as a narrowing filter.\n\n`status` defaults to `OPEN`, which is the **superset**: a\nsettled-but-unredeemed winner still holds its tokens, so it is an open\nposition whose condition resolved. `REDEEMABLE` narrows to that subset, and\neach row echoes its own `status`.\n\nResume contract: a `next_cursor` binds the `status`/`sortBy`/`sortDirection`\nthe walk started with. To follow it, send `cursor` together with the same\n`user` or `condition` anchor used on the first page; a bare `?cursor=` request\nreturns 400. The token is the authority on the spine and the total order,\nand the handler adopts all three from it. Restating them is allowed and\nmust agree;\n**explicitly** contradicting one is a 400, because replaying an anchor under\na different spine or order would silently walk a different result set.\nOmitting them is not a contradiction; a defaulted `status` is the absence of\na choice, not a request for `OPEN`.\n\nA malformed `condition` id is a `400` naming the value; a\nwell-formed one that matches nothing serves an empty `data` array, which\nis the meaningful zero-state; absence means the market is not servable,\nand only that."])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"4d:T464,"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"The ranked board of realized PnL, combos included.\n\n`?time_period=` is `day` (default), `week`, `month` or `all`; `?category=`\nis `overall` (default) or a market category; `?sort_by=` picks the `PNL`\n(default) or `VOLUME` board. Deeper pages come only from `?cursor=`.\n\nA cursor **pins the board it was minted on**; sort, window and category;\nso following it needs no params at all, and restating a different one is a\n`400` rather than a silent re-point (the builders-board pattern).\n\n`?user=` answers a different question; one wallet's standing, carrying\n**both** the PnL and volume ranks in a single object rather than a page. A\nrank of `0` there means unranked for that board, not first. `sort_by`,\n`limit` and `cursor` do not apply to that arm.\n\n**`rank` ties and skips**: tied users share a rank and the next one jumps,\nso a partition's highest rank approaches its row count. Page with the\ncursor; never compute a page from a rank.\n\nFinite windows (day/week/month) serve the MARKED equity change net of\nflows; they move with unrealized marks; `all` is the realized-only\nlifetime ledger. `volume` is in shares, not USDC."])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"4e:T679,"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"Combo positions for a user, in the standard\n`{ data, pagination }` envelope.\n\nSorts: `FIRST_ENTRY` (default) | `ENTRY_COST` (+ `CURRENT_VALUE` alias) |\n`UPDATED`, each with `sort_direction`. `FIRST_ENTRY DESC` pages by the\ntwo-state keyset anchor `(first_entry_at_micros, combo_condition_id,\noutcome_index)` (NULL micros = the NULL tail); `UPDATED ASC` by the\nsingle-state `(updated_at_micros, …)` anchor; every other combination by an\noffset-shaped token. The cursor binds sort + direction and the resume\nADOPTS them, so a replay cannot flip or re-sort the walk mid-stream.\n\nIt binds the cohort; `user`/`status`/`condition`/`updated_after`/\n`updated_before`; the same way: following a\npage needs nothing but `?user=` (always required here) and `?cursor=`, and\nrestating a filter is allowed but must agree. Omitting one is not a\ncontradiction, it is the absence of a choice; **contradicting** one is a\n400, because the token's walk state only means anything against the cohort\nit was minted on.\n\nIncremental sync: `updated_after`/`updated_before` are an INCLUSIVE\nepoch-second window on `updated_at`. Without a `status` filter, either\nbound switches the response to the mirror-complete sync view (every live\nrow, not only held ones); a `status` filter keeps its own visibility. The\nupper end is always capped by a short stability ceiling (~90s behind now)\nso a mirror never reads rows that may still move. Pair with\n`sortBy=UPDATED\u0026sortDirection=ASC` for the stable sync order.\n\nA malformed `condition` combo condition id is a `400` naming the value; a\nwell-formed one that matches nothing serves an empty `data` array, which\nis the meaningful zero-state."])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"4f:T89f,"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"Get the global perpetuals leaderboard, ranked by PnL, notional volume, or\ncurrent account value across all instruments.\n\nWindows are anchored to calendar UTC boundaries: `day` starts at 00:00 UTC\ntoday, `week` at Monday 00:00 UTC, `month` at the first of the month\n00:00 UTC, and `all` at exchange launch.\n\nPnL is realized PnL minus trading fees plus funding payments, consistent\nwith the account PnL endpoint; unrealized PnL is excluded. Notional is the\nUSD value of all fills in the window. Every entry carries both metrics;\n`rank` is the position under the requested `sort_by`.\n\nPnL, notional, and account value are raw numeric strings from the engine.\nAccount value is current equity (collateral value plus unrealized PnL).\nThe background census advances by at most 8,192 accounts on each 60-second\npoller tick, so a full publication can span multiple ticks as the account\npopulation grows. For account-value sorting, `timestamp` is the earlier of\nthe published census start and the historical window's computation time,\nso stale membership and PnL remain observable if a historical rebuild fails.\nWhen sorting by account value, the requested window still determines which\naccounts and historical PnL/notional metrics are included, while the\nranking uses their current equity. Accounts whose equity cannot be computed\nare excluded from that ranking. When unrealized PnL is unavailable (for\nexample, due to stale marks), the display field falls back to collateral\nvalue on PnL/notional entries and address lookups; it does not establish an\nequity rank. `total` counts accounts with published equity in that window.\n`sort_by=account_value` returns 503 while the first completed census is\nwarming. PnL and notional rankings remain available during that warm-up.\nClients are responsible for decimal and currency presentation formatting.\n\nRankings are recomputed periodically; `timestamp` is the computation time.\nReturns 25 entries by default and at most 100 per request; only the top\n1000 ranks are pageable (`offset + limit` must not exceed 1000).\n\nProvide `address` to additionally return that account's row regardless of\nrank. An address with no activity in the window returns zero metrics and\nno rank.\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"50:T4b1,"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"Get every fill in a registered account's current open position cycle for\none instrument. A cycle begins when the position opens from flat or flips\ndirection. For a flip, every fill from the flipping engine event belongs\nto the new cycle so a fill is never split between cycles.\n\nReturns an empty page when the account has no open position for the\ninstrument. Maximum of 100 entries returned per request. Results are\nordered by time; use `sort` to choose newest-first (`desc`, default) or\noldest-first (`asc`). To page through more than 100 fills, pass the opaque\n`cursor` returned by the previous page and keep `sort` unchanged. Each page\nverifies that the cursor still describes the account's current position\ncycle. If that position changes while pagination is in progress, the\ncursor returns `400` and pagination must restart from the first page.\n\nCycle discovery for a position inherited from a gateway snapshot is\nlimited to 250,000 account-history rows. A cycle older than that bound\nreturns `413` rather than allowing a public request to run an unbounded\nClickHouse scan. Positions opened or flipped after gateway startup carry\ntheir cycle boundary directly and do not use this discovery scan.\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"51:T672,"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"Update leverage for an instrument.\n\nEach setting resolves independently: explicit per-instrument setting, then\nexchange-managed account-group default, then instrument maximum leverage and\nisolated margin. Group leverage is capped at the instrument maximum; a group\ncross default resolves to isolated on isolated-only instruments. Group defaults\napply to new listings and never overwrite explicit settings.\nThis operation sets both settings explicitly; GET /v1/account/config reports\nresolved values. Submit the current resolved pair to preserve it against later\ngroup changes. Leverage bounds and BLP locks also apply to unchanged values.\nSet your preferred leverage and margin mode after listing and before placing\nyour first order. An unknown instrument ID (never listed) is rejected with\n`instrument_not_found`; a disabled instrument is not rejected merely because\nit is disabled.\n\nMargin mode can change only when the account has no position and no open\norders in that instrument, including orders awaiting risk approval or execution.\nClose the position and cancel all orders before switching between isolated\nand cross margin. A position blocks a mode change with `position_exists`;\nopen orders block it with `open_orders_exist`. Leverage changes within the\nsame mode remain subject to leverage limits and margin checks. Leverage must\nbe positive (`lev: 0` returns 400); exceeding the instrument maximum returns\n`invalid_leverage`. BLP-subscribed instruments reject leverage or mode updates\nwith `blp_leverage_locked`; unsubscribe before changing the configuration.\n\nRequires proxy signature, see [proxy signing](/http/signing#2-proxy-signing).\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"52:T819,"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"Update leverage for up to 100 unique instruments. Updates are processed\nsequentially and are not atomic. If only some responses arrive before the\ngateway deadline, missing item results use `internal_error`; whether those\nupdates applied is unknown. If no responses arrive, the request returns\n503 — retryable, since each update is an idempotent leverage/margin-type\nset that converges to the same value whether or not the original attempt\nwas admitted.\n\nEach setting resolves independently: explicit per-instrument setting, then\nexchange-managed account-group default, then instrument maximum leverage and\nisolated margin. Group leverage is capped at the instrument maximum; a group\ncross default resolves to isolated on isolated-only instruments. Group defaults\napply to new listings and never overwrite explicit settings.\nThis operation sets both settings explicitly; GET /v1/account/config reports\nresolved values. Submit the current resolved pair to preserve it against later\ngroup changes. Leverage bounds and BLP locks also apply to unchanged values.\nSet your preferred leverage and margin mode after listing and before placing\nyour first order. An unknown instrument ID (never listed) is rejected with\n`instrument_not_found`; a disabled instrument is not rejected merely because\nit is disabled.\n\nMargin mode can change only when the account has no position and no open\norders in that instrument, including orders awaiting risk approval or execution.\nClose the position and cancel all orders before switching between isolated\nand cross margin. A position blocks a mode change with `position_exists`;\nopen orders block it with `open_orders_exist`. Leverage changes within the\nsame mode remain subject to leverage limits and margin checks. Leverage must\nbe positive (`lev: 0` returns 400); exceeding the instrument maximum returns\n`invalid_leverage`. BLP-subscribed instruments reject leverage or mode updates\nwith `blp_leverage_locked`; unsubscribe before changing the configuration.\n\nRequires proxy signature, see [Update Leverage](/perps/trading#update-leverage).\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"19:[\"$\",\"$L47\",null,{\"scopedNav\":{\"global\":null,\"languages\":[{\"language\":\"en\",\"banner\":{\"content\":\"Data API v2 is live. Data API v1 is retired on October 24, 2026 — see the [migration guide](/migrate/data-api-v1-to-v2).\",\"dismissible\":true},\"tabs\":[{\"tab\":\"Predictions\",\"groups\":[{\"group\":\"Getting Started\",\"icon\":\"https://mintlify.s3.us-west-1.amazonaws.com/polymarket-292d1b1b/images/icons/nav/book.svg\",\"pages\":[{\"title\":\"Overview\",\"description\":\"Build on the world's largest prediction market. Trade, integrate, and access real-time market data with the Polymarket API.\",\"mode\":\"frame\",\"href\":\"\"},{\"title\":\"Polymarket 101\",\"description\":\"An intro to Polymarket - the world's largest prediction market\",\"href\":\"/polymarket-101\"},{\"group\":\"SDKs \u0026 APIs\",\"root\":{\"title\":\"SDKs \u0026 APIs\",\"description\":\"Choose how to integrate with Polymarket.\",\"href\":\"/getting-started/sdks-apis\"},\"pages\":[{\"title\":\"TypeScript SDK\",\"description\":\"Get started with the unified Polymarket TypeScript SDK.\",\"hideFooterPagination\":true,\"href\":\"/getting-started/typescript\"},{\"title\":\"Python SDK\",\"description\":\"Get started with the unified Polymarket Python SDK.\",\"hideFooterPagination\":true,\"href\":\"/getting-started/python\"},{\"title\":\"API\",\"description\":\"Build directly with Polymarket REST APIs and WebSocket streams.\",\"hideFooterPagination\":true,\"href\":\"/getting-started/api\"}]}]},{\"group\":\"Core Concepts\",\"icon\":\"https://mintlify.s3.us-west-1.amazonaws.com/polymarket-292d1b1b/images/icons/nav/layers.svg\",\"pages\":[{\"title\":\"Markets \u0026 Events\",\"description\":\"Understanding the fundamental building blocks of Polymarket\",\"href\":\"/concepts/markets-events\"},{\"title\":\"Negative Risk Markets\",\"description\":\"Capital-efficient trading for multi-outcome events\",\"href\":\"/concepts/negative-risk\"},{\"title\":\"Prices \u0026 Orderbook\",\"description\":\"How prices work and how the order book enables peer-to-peer trading\",\"href\":\"/concepts/prices-orderbook\"},{\"title\":\"Positions \u0026 Tokens\",\"description\":\"Understanding outcome tokens and how positions work on Polymarket\",\"href\":\"/concepts/positions-tokens\"},{\"title\":\"Polymarket USD\",\"description\":\"pUSD — the collateral token used for all trading on Polymarket\",\"href\":\"/concepts/pusd\"},{\"title\":\"Order Lifecycle\",\"description\":\"Understanding how orders flow from creation to settlement\",\"href\":\"/concepts/order-lifecycle\"},{\"title\":\"Resolution\",\"description\":\"How markets are resolved and winning positions redeemed\",\"href\":\"/concepts/resolution\"}]},{\"group\":\"Market Data\",\"icon\":\"https://mintlify.s3.us-west-1.amazonaws.com/polymarket-292d1b1b/images/icons/nav/paper.svg\",\"pages\":[{\"title\":\"Overview\",\"description\":\"Learn how Polymarket organizes market data and where to begin.\",\"href\":\"/market-data/overview\"},{\"title\":\"Discover Markets\",\"description\":\"Learn how to find and filter events and markets and explore related metadata.\",\"href\":\"/market-data/discover-markets\"},{\"title\":\"Market Details\",\"description\":\"Understand the structure and state of a Polymarket market.\",\"href\":\"/market-data/market-details\"},{\"title\":\"Prices and Order Books\",\"description\":\"Learn how prices and order books represent trading activity on Polymarket.\",\"href\":\"/market-data/prices-order-books\"},{\"title\":\"Analytics\",\"description\":\"Understand activity and performance across Polymarket.\",\"href\":\"/market-data/public-analytics\"},{\"title\":\"Real-Time Data\",\"description\":\"Keep market data current with Polymarket's real-time feeds.\",\"href\":\"/market-data/realtime-data\"}]},{\"group\":\"Trading\",\"icon\":\"https://mintlify.s3.us-west-1.amazonaws.com/polymarket-292d1b1b/images/icons/nav/chart.svg\",\"pages\":[{\"title\":\"Overview\",\"description\":\"Understand how orders, settlement, and positions fit together on Polymarket.\",\"hideFooterPagination\":true,\"href\":\"/trading/overview\"},{\"title\":\"Place Your First Order\",\"description\":\"Learn how to authenticate with the CLOB and submit your first market order.\",\"href\":\"/trading/quickstart\"},{\"title\":\"Wallets and Authentication\",\"description\":\"Connect or create a Polymarket account for trading.\",\"href\":\"/trading/wallets-auth\"},{\"title\":\"Session Keys\",\"description\":\"Authorize a separate signer for scoped, time-limited Deposit Wallet trading.\",\"tag\":\"Beta\",\"href\":\"/trading/session-keys\"},{\"title\":\"Place Orders\",\"description\":\"Learn how to place orders and control how they execute\",\"href\":\"/trading/place-orders\"},{\"title\":\"Manage Orders\",\"description\":\"Learn how to track and manage orders after submitting them.\",\"href\":\"/trading/manage-orders\"},{\"title\":\"Real-Time Order Updates\",\"description\":\"React to authenticated order and trade activity as it happens.\",\"href\":\"/trading/realtime-order-updates\"},{\"group\":\"Positions\",\"pages\":[{\"title\":\"How Positions Work\",\"description\":\"Understand the onchain token mechanics that power Polymarket positions.\",\"href\":\"/trading/positions/how-positions-work\"},{\"title\":\"Manage Positions\",\"description\":\"Learn how to manage outcome-token inventory from creation through redemption.\",\"href\":\"/trading/positions/manage\"},{\"title\":\"Combinatorial Positions\",\"description\":\"Multi-leg positions built from existing Polymarket outcomes\",\"href\":\"/trading/positions/combinatorial\"}]},{\"group\":\"Combos\",\"pages\":[{\"title\":\"How Combos Work\",\"description\":\"Understand Combo positions and the RFQ flow for multi-leg markets\",\"mode\":\"wide\",\"href\":\"/trading/combos/overview\"},{\"title\":\"Requesters\",\"description\":\"Request Combo quotes and execute accepted trades\",\"tag\":\"New\",\"href\":\"/trading/combos/requesters\"},{\"title\":\"Market Makers\",\"description\":\"Build a market maker integration for pricing and executing Combos\",\"href\":\"/trading/combos/market-makers\"},{\"title\":\"Combos for Builders\",\"description\":\"Request and execute Combo quotes for users through the Builder Gateway\",\"tag\":\"New\",\"href\":\"/trading/combos/builders\"},{\"title\":\"Collateral Return\",\"description\":\"Release pUSD from compatible Combo positions before resolution\",\"tag\":\"New\",\"href\":\"/trading/combos/collateral-return\"}]},{\"title\":\"Wallet Activity\",\"description\":\"Track the positions and activity associated with a Polymarket wallet.\",\"href\":\"/trading/wallet-activity\"},{\"title\":\"Fees\",\"description\":\"Understanding trading fees on Polymarket\",\"href\":\"/trading/fees\"},{\"title\":\"Market Making\",\"description\":\"Guidance for operating a market-making system on Polymarket.\",\"href\":\"/trading/market-making\"},{\"title\":\"Matching Engine Restarts\",\"description\":\"Maintenance windows, restart handling, and post-restart post-only mode\",\"href\":\"/trading/matching-engine\"},{\"group\":\"Bridge\",\"pages\":[{\"title\":\"Deposit\",\"description\":\"Bridge assets from any supported chain to fund your Polymarket account\",\"href\":\"/trading/bridge/deposit\"},{\"title\":\"Supported Assets\",\"description\":\"Chains and tokens supported for deposits to Polymarket\",\"href\":\"/trading/bridge/supported-assets\"},{\"title\":\"Quote\",\"description\":\"Preview fees and estimated output for deposits and withdrawals\",\"href\":\"/trading/bridge/quote\"},{\"title\":\"Withdraw\",\"description\":\"Bridge pUSD from Polymarket to any supported chain\",\"href\":\"/trading/bridge/withdraw\"},{\"title\":\"Transaction Status\",\"description\":\"Track bridge deposits and withdrawals through completion\",\"href\":\"/trading/bridge/status\"}]}]},{\"group\":\"Programs\",\"icon\":\"https://mintlify.s3.us-west-1.amazonaws.com/polymarket-292d1b1b/images/icons/nav/trophy.svg\",\"pages\":[{\"title\":\"Taker Rebate Program\",\"description\":\"Climb the tiers and earn daily pUSD rebates as you trade\",\"href\":\"/programs/taker-rebates\"},{\"title\":\"Maker Rebates Program\",\"description\":\"Earn daily pUSD rebates by providing liquidity on Polymarket\",\"href\":\"/programs/maker-rebates\"},{\"title\":\"Liquidity Rewards\",\"description\":\"Earn rewards for providing liquidity on Polymarket\",\"href\":\"/programs/liquidity-rewards\"},{\"group\":\"Builder Program\",\"pages\":[{\"title\":\"Overview\",\"description\":\"Build applications that route orders through Polymarket\",\"href\":\"/programs/builders/overview\"},{\"title\":\"Builder Fees\",\"description\":\"How builders earn fees on orders routed through their applications, and how to integrate.\",\"href\":\"/programs/builders/fees\"},{\"title\":\"Tiers\",\"description\":\"Rate limits, rewards, and how to upgrade\",\"href\":\"/programs/builders/tiers\"}]},{\"title\":\"Referral Program\",\"description\":\"Refer traders to Polymarket and earn daily pUSD rewards\",\"href\":\"/programs/referral-program\"}]},{\"group\":\"Migration Guides\",\"icon\":\"https://mintlify.s3.us-west-1.amazonaws.com/polymarket-292d1b1b/images/icons/nav/compass.svg\",\"pages\":[{\"title\":\"Migrate from Data API v1 to v2\",\"description\":\"Move an integration from the original Data API routes to their v2 counterparts: the route mapping, the contract changes, and what stays on v1.\",\"href\":\"/migrate/data-api-v1-to-v2\"},{\"title\":\"Migrate from old SDKs to Unified SDKs\",\"description\":\"Move an existing Polymarket integration to the unified SDKs.\",\"href\":\"/migrate/clob-sdk-to-unified-sdk\"}]},{\"group\":\"Resources\",\"icon\":\"https://mintlify.s3.us-west-1.amazonaws.com/polymarket-292d1b1b/images/icons/nav/book-search.svg\",\"pages\":[{\"title\":\"Contracts\",\"description\":\"All Polymarket smart contract addresses, audits, and security resources\",\"href\":\"/resources/contracts\"},{\"title\":\"Data Resources\",\"description\":\"Access Polymarket on-chain activity for data \u0026 analytics\",\"href\":\"/resources/blockchain-data\"},{\"title\":\"Error Codes\",\"description\":\"Complete reference for CLOB API error responses\",\"href\":\"/resources/error-codes\"}]}]},{\"tab\":\"Perps\",\"pages\":[{\"title\":\"Perps\",\"href\":\"/perps/overview\"}]},{\"tab\":\"API Reference\",\"dropdowns\":[{\"dropdown\":\"Predictions\",\"icon\":\"chart-pie\",\"pages\":[{\"title\":\"Overview\",\"description\":\"Explore the APIs available for building with Polymarket Predictions.\",\"hideFooterPagination\":true,\"href\":\"/api-reference/predictions/overview\"},{\"title\":\"Rate Limits\",\"description\":\"Cloudflare IP-based request limits for Polymarket APIs\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/rate-limits\"},{\"title\":\"CLOB Trading Rate Limits\",\"description\":\"Per-signer token-bucket limits for CLOB order and cancellation requests\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/trading-rate-limits\"},{\"title\":\"Geographic Restrictions\",\"description\":\"Check geographic restrictions before placing orders on the Polymarket API\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/geoblock\"},{\"title\":\"Get data freshness\",\"description\":\"$48\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"openapi\":\"https:/data-api.polymarket.com/v2/openapi.json get /v2/status\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/service/get-data-freshness\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"group\":\"Events\",\"pages\":[{\"title\":\"List events (keyset pagination)\",\"description\":\"Returns events using cursor-based (keyset) pagination for stable, efficient paging through large result sets. Use `next_cursor` from each response as `after_cursor` in the next request. The `offset` parameter is explicitly rejected; use `after_cursor` instead.\\n\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"openapi\":\"/api-spec/gamma-openapi.yaml get /events/keyset\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/events/list-events-keyset-pagination\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"List events\",\"description\":null,\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"openapi\":\"/api-spec/gamma-openapi.yaml get /events\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/events/list-events\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"Get event by id\",\"description\":null,\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"openapi\":\"/api-spec/gamma-openapi.yaml get /events/{id}\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/events/get-event-by-id\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"Get event by slug\",\"description\":null,\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"openapi\":\"/api-spec/gamma-openapi.yaml get /events/slug/{slug}\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/events/get-event-by-slug\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"Get event tags\",\"description\":null,\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"openapi\":\"/api-spec/gamma-openapi.yaml get /events/{id}/tags\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/events/get-event-tags\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true}]},{\"group\":\"Markets\",\"pages\":[{\"title\":\"List markets (keyset pagination)\",\"description\":\"Returns markets using cursor-based (keyset) pagination for stable, efficient paging through large result sets. Use `next_cursor` from each response as `after_cursor` in the next request. The `offset` parameter is explicitly rejected; use `after_cursor` instead.\\n\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"openapi\":\"/api-spec/gamma-openapi.yaml get /markets/keyset\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/markets/list-markets-keyset-pagination\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"List markets\",\"description\":null,\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"openapi\":\"/api-spec/gamma-openapi.yaml get /markets\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/markets/list-markets\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"Get market by id\",\"description\":null,\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"openapi\":\"/api-spec/gamma-openapi.yaml get /markets/{id}\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/markets/get-market-by-id\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"Get market by slug\",\"description\":null,\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"openapi\":\"/api-spec/gamma-openapi.yaml get /markets/slug/{slug}\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/markets/get-market-by-slug\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"Get market tags by id\",\"description\":null,\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"openapi\":\"/api-spec/gamma-openapi.yaml get /markets/{id}/tags\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/markets/get-market-tags-by-id\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"Get market by token\",\"description\":\"Returns the parent market for a given token ID. Useful when you have\\na token ID and need to resolve its parent market without knowing the\\ncondition ID in advance.\\n\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"openapi\":\"/api-spec/clob-openapi.yaml get /markets-by-token/{token_id}\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/markets/get-market-by-token\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"List a market's top holders\",\"description\":\"$49\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"openapi\":\"https:/data-api.polymarket.com/v2/openapi.json get /v2/holders\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/markets/list-a-markets-top-holders\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"Get open interest\",\"description\":\"Priced gross open interest per market.\\n\\nPass `?condition=` as a comma-separated list of condition ids (aliases `condition_id` / `conditionId`, matching the feeds); omit it for the single\\nglobal figure (`condition_id = \\\"GLOBAL\\\"`, still a one-element array).\\nEvery requested id that resolves to a servable market (indexed, active,\\nnot archived; any id family) returns a row, with `value: 0` when\\nnothing is held; an id absent from `data` did not resolve to a servable\\nmarket. A malformed id is a `400` naming the value, so absence carries that\\none meaning and nothing else. Unlike the feeds this is not paginated;\\n`data` is the row array with no `pagination`.\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"openapi\":\"https:/data-api.polymarket.com/v2/openapi.json get /v2/oi\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/markets/get-open-interest\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"Get live volume for an event\",\"description\":\"Cumulative one-side (taker) volume per market.\\n\\nPass `?event_id=` as a comma-separated list of integer event ids (aliases `id` / `eventId`); every market under those events is returned, `taker_volume`\\ndescending, with `taker_volume_total` their sum. A list spans events. Unlike the\\nfeeds this is not paginated; `data` is\\nthe object with no `pagination`.\\n\\nUnparseable ids are ignored; a request whose ids are *all* unparseable is a\\n400 rather than an empty 200, so a typo cannot read as \\\"no volume\\\". Ids are\\nsorted and deduplicated before the lookup, so `?event_id=20,10` and\\n`?event_id=10,20` are the same request and share a cache entry.\\n\\nAt most 20 distinct event ids per request, the same selector ceiling the\\n`condition=` lists carry: every named event contributes all of its markets\\nto a single aggregation, so the list is what sizes the request.\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"openapi\":\"https:/data-api.polymarket.com/v2/openapi.json get /v2/live-volume\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/markets/get-live-volume-for-an-event\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"Get resolution state\",\"description\":\"Complete resolution state by one selector family.\\n\\nSupply exactly one of `question_id`, `condition`, or `event_id`. Condition and\\nevent selectors accept comma-separated values and return condition-grain\\nrows in deterministic order, preferring native V2 lifecycle, then UMA\\nlifecycle, then terminal CTF state. Misses return `{ \\\"data\\\": [] }`.\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"openapi\":\"https:/data-api.polymarket.com/v2/openapi.json get /v2/resolutions\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/markets/get-resolution-state\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"Get simplified markets\",\"description\":null,\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"openapi\":\"/api-spec/clob-openapi.yaml get /simplified-markets\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/markets/get-simplified-markets\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"Get sampling markets\",\"description\":null,\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"openapi\":\"/api-spec/clob-openapi.yaml get /sampling-markets\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/markets/get-sampling-markets\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"Get sampling simplified markets\",\"description\":null,\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"openapi\":\"/api-spec/clob-openapi.yaml get /sampling-simplified-markets\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/markets/get-sampling-simplified-markets\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true}]},{\"group\":\"Orderbook \u0026 Pricing\",\"pages\":[{\"title\":\"Get order book\",\"description\":\"Retrieves the order book summary for a specific token ID.\\nIncludes bids, asks, market details, and last trade price.\\n\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"openapi\":\"/api-spec/clob-openapi.yaml get /book\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/market-data/get-order-book\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"Get order books (request body)\",\"description\":\"Retrieves order book summaries for multiple token IDs using a request body.\\n\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"openapi\":\"/api-spec/clob-openapi.yaml post /books\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/market-data/get-order-books-request-body\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"Get market price\",\"description\":\"Retrieves the best market price for a specific token ID and side (bid or ask).\\nReturns the best bid price for BUY side or best ask price for SELL side.\\n\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"openapi\":\"/api-spec/clob-openapi.yaml get /price\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/market-data/get-market-price\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"Get market prices (query parameters)\",\"description\":\"Retrieves market prices for multiple token IDs and sides using query parameters.\\n\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"openapi\":\"/api-spec/clob-openapi.yaml get /prices\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/market-data/get-market-prices-query-parameters\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"Get market prices (request body)\",\"description\":\"Retrieves market prices for multiple token IDs and sides using a request body.\\nEach request must include both token_id and side.\\n\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"openapi\":\"/api-spec/clob-openapi.yaml post /prices\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/market-data/get-market-prices-request-body\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"Get midpoint price\",\"description\":\"Retrieves the midpoint price for a specific token ID.\\nThe midpoint is calculated as the average of the best bid and best ask prices.\\n\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"openapi\":\"/api-spec/clob-openapi.yaml get /midpoint\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/data/get-midpoint-price\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"Get midpoint prices (query parameters)\",\"description\":\"Retrieves midpoint prices for multiple token IDs using query parameters.\\nThe midpoint is calculated as the average of the best bid and best ask prices.\\n\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"openapi\":\"/api-spec/clob-openapi.yaml get /midpoints\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/market-data/get-midpoint-prices-query-parameters\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"Get midpoint prices (request body)\",\"description\":\"Retrieves midpoint prices for multiple token IDs using a request body.\\nThe midpoint is calculated as the average of the best bid and best ask prices.\\n\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"openapi\":\"/api-spec/clob-openapi.yaml post /midpoints\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/market-data/get-midpoint-prices-request-body\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"Get spread\",\"description\":\"Retrieves the spread for a specific token ID.\\nThe spread is the difference between the best ask and best bid prices.\\n\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"openapi\":\"/api-spec/clob-openapi.yaml get /spread\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/market-data/get-spread\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"Get spreads\",\"description\":\"Retrieves spreads for multiple token IDs.\\nThe spread is the difference between the best ask and best bid prices.\\n\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"openapi\":\"/api-spec/clob-openapi.yaml post /spreads\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/market-data/get-spreads\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"Get last trade price\",\"description\":\"Retrieves the last trade price and side for a specific token ID.\\nReturns default values of \\\"0.5\\\" for price and empty string for side if no trades found.\\n\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"openapi\":\"/api-spec/clob-openapi.yaml get /last-trade-price\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/market-data/get-last-trade-price\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"Get last trade prices (query parameters)\",\"description\":\"Retrieves last trade prices for multiple token IDs using query parameters.\\nMaximum 500 token IDs can be requested per call.\\n\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"openapi\":\"/api-spec/clob-openapi.yaml get /last-trades-prices\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/market-data/get-last-trade-prices-query-parameters\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"Get last trade prices (request body)\",\"description\":\"Retrieves last trade prices for multiple token IDs using a request body.\\nMaximum 500 token IDs can be requested per call.\\n\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"openapi\":\"/api-spec/clob-openapi.yaml post /last-trades-prices\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/market-data/get-last-trade-prices-request-body\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"Get prices history\",\"description\":\"Retrieve historical price data for a market.\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"openapi\":\"/api-spec/clob-openapi.yaml get /prices-history\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/markets/get-prices-history\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"Get a token's price history\",\"description\":\"$4a\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"openapi\":\"https:/data-api.polymarket.com/v2/openapi.json get /v2/prices-history\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/markets/get-a-tokens-price-history\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"Get batch prices history\",\"description\":\"Retrieve historical price data for multiple markets in a single request.\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"openapi\":\"/api-spec/clob-openapi.yaml post /batch-prices-history\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/markets/get-batch-prices-history\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"Get fee rate\",\"description\":\"Retrieves the base fee rate for a specific token ID.\\nThe fee rate can be provided either as a query parameter or as a path parameter.\\n\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"openapi\":\"/api-spec/clob-openapi.yaml get /fee-rate\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/market-data/get-fee-rate\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"Get fee rate by path parameter\",\"description\":\"Retrieves the base fee rate for a specific token ID using the token ID as a path parameter.\\n\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"openapi\":\"/api-spec/clob-openapi.yaml get /fee-rate/{token_id}\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/market-data/get-fee-rate-by-path-parameter\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"Get tick size\",\"description\":\"Retrieves the minimum tick size (price increment) for a specific token ID.\\nThe tick size can be provided either as a query parameter or as a path parameter.\\n\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"openapi\":\"/api-spec/clob-openapi.yaml get /tick-size\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/market-data/get-tick-size\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"Get tick size by path parameter\",\"description\":\"Retrieves the minimum tick size (price increment) for a specific token ID using the token ID as a path parameter.\\n\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"openapi\":\"/api-spec/clob-openapi.yaml get /tick-size/{token_id}\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/market-data/get-tick-size-by-path-parameter\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"Get CLOB market info\",\"description\":\"Returns all CLOB-level parameters for a market in a single call —\\ntokens, tick size, base fees, rewards, RFQ status, and fee details.\\n\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"openapi\":\"/api-spec/clob-openapi.yaml get /clob-markets/{condition_id}\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/markets/get-clob-market-info\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"Get server time\",\"description\":\"Returns the current Unix timestamp of the server.\\nThis can be used to synchronize client time with server time.\\n\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"openapi\":\"/api-spec/clob-openapi.yaml get /time\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/data/get-server-time\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true}]},{\"group\":\"Orders\",\"pages\":[{\"title\":\"Post a new order\",\"description\":\"Creates a new order in the order book\\n\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"openapi\":\"/api-spec/clob-openapi.yaml post /order\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/trade/post-a-new-order\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"Cancel single order\",\"description\":\"Cancels a single order by its ID. Works even in cancel-only mode.\\n\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"openapi\":\"/api-spec/clob-openapi.yaml delete /order\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/trade/cancel-single-order\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"Get single order by ID\",\"description\":\"Retrieves a specific order by its ID (order hash) for the authenticated user, including canceled or fully matched orders.\\nBuilder-authenticated clients can also use this endpoint to retrieve orders attributed to their builder account.\\n\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"openapi\":\"/api-spec/clob-openapi.yaml get /data/order/{orderID}\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/trade/get-single-order-by-id\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"Post multiple orders\",\"description\":\"Creates multiple new orders in the order book. Orders are processed in parallel.\\nMaximum 15 orders per request.\\n\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"openapi\":\"/api-spec/clob-openapi.yaml post /orders\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/trade/post-multiple-orders\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"Get user orders\",\"description\":\"Retrieves live orders for the authenticated user. Returns paginated results.\\nFiltering by id returns that order regardless of status, including canceled or fully matched orders.\\nBuilder-authenticated clients can also use this endpoint to retrieve orders attributed to their builder account.\\n\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"openapi\":\"/api-spec/clob-openapi.yaml get /data/orders\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/trade/get-user-orders\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"Cancel multiple orders\",\"description\":\"Cancels multiple orders by their IDs. Maximum 1000 orders per request.\\nDuplicate order IDs in the request are automatically ignored.\\nWorks even in cancel-only mode.\\n\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"openapi\":\"/api-spec/clob-openapi.yaml delete /orders\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/trade/cancel-multiple-orders\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"Cancel all orders\",\"description\":\"Cancels all open orders for the authenticated user. Works even in cancel-only mode.\\n\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"openapi\":\"/api-spec/clob-openapi.yaml delete /cancel-all\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/trade/cancel-all-orders\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"Cancel orders for a market\",\"description\":\"Cancels all open orders for the authenticated user in a specific market (condition) and asset.\\nWorks even in cancel-only mode.\\n\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"openapi\":\"/api-spec/clob-openapi.yaml delete /cancel-market-orders\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/trade/cancel-orders-for-a-market\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"Get order scoring status\",\"description\":\"Checks if a specific order is currently scoring for rewards.\\n\\nAn order is considered \\\"scoring\\\" if it meets all the criteria for earning maker rewards:\\n- The order is live on a rewards-eligible market\\n- The order meets the minimum size requirements\\n- The order is within the valid spread range\\n- The order has been live for the required duration\\n\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"openapi\":\"/api-spec/clob-openapi.yaml get /order-scoring\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/trade/get-order-scoring-status\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"Send heartbeat\",\"description\":\"Sends a heartbeat signal to maintain active session status.\\nIf heartbeats are not sent regularly, all open orders for the user will be automatically canceled.\\nThis is useful for automated trading systems that need to ensure orders are canceled\\nif the system becomes unresponsive.\\n\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"openapi\":\"/api-spec/clob-openapi.yaml post /heartbeats\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/trade/send-heartbeat\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true}]},{\"group\":\"Trades\",\"pages\":[{\"title\":\"List trades\",\"description\":\"Keyset-paginated trade feed in the standard\\n`{ data, pagination }` envelope.\\n\\nPass `?cursor=` from a prior response's `next_cursor` to fetch the next page;\\nit carries both the page size and the `(block_timestamp, sequence_id)` seek\\nanchor, so deep pages cost the same as shallow ones.\\n\\nA malformed `condition` id is a `400` naming the value; a\\nwell-formed one that matches nothing serves an empty `data` array, which\\nis the meaningful zero-state; absence means the market is not servable,\\nand only that.\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"openapi\":\"https:/data-api.polymarket.com/v2/openapi.json get /v2/trades\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/feeds/list-trades\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"Get trades\",\"description\":\"Retrieves trades for the authenticated user. Returns paginated results.\\nRequires readonly or level 2 API key authentication.\\n\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"openapi\":\"/api-spec/clob-openapi.yaml get /data/trades\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/trade/get-trades\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"Get builder trades\",\"description\":\"Retrieves trades attributed to a builder code.\\n\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"openapi\":\"/api-spec/clob-openapi.yaml get /builder/trades\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/trade/get-builder-trades\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true}]},{\"group\":\"Rebates\",\"pages\":[{\"title\":\"Get current rebated fees for a maker\",\"description\":\"Returns the current rebated fees for a maker address on a given date.\\n\\nEach entry includes the condition ID, asset address, and the USDC amount rebated.\\n\\nThis endpoint does not require authentication.\\n\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"openapi\":\"/api-spec/clob-openapi.yaml get /rebates/current\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/rebates/get-current-rebated-fees-for-a-maker\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true}]},{\"group\":\"Rewards\",\"pages\":[{\"title\":\"Get current active rewards configurations\",\"description\":\"Returns all current active rewards configurations grouped by market.\\n\\nWhen `sponsored=true`, returns sponsored reward configurations instead.\\n\\nResults are paginated (500 items per page). Use next_cursor to fetch subsequent pages.\\nA next_cursor value of \\\"LTE=\\\" indicates the last page.\\n\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"openapi\":\"/api-spec/clob-openapi.yaml get /rewards/markets/current\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/rewards/get-current-active-rewards-configurations\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"Get raw rewards for a specific market\",\"description\":\"Returns an array of present and future rewards configured on a market.\\n\\nWhen `sponsored=true`, sponsored daily rates are folded into each config's\\n`rate_per_day` .\\n\\nResults are paginated (100 items per page). Use next_cursor to fetch subsequent pages.\\nA next_cursor value of \\\"LTE=\\\" indicates the last page.\\n\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"openapi\":\"/api-spec/clob-openapi.yaml get /rewards/markets/{condition_id}\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/rewards/get-raw-rewards-for-a-specific-market\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"Get multiple markets with rewards\",\"description\":\"Returns a list of active markets with their reward configurations.\\nSupports text search, tag filtering, numeric filters, and sorting.\\n\\nResults are paginated (100 items per page by default). Use next_cursor to fetch subsequent pages.\\nA next_cursor value of \\\"LTE=\\\" indicates the last page.\\n\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"openapi\":\"/api-spec/clob-openapi.yaml get /rewards/markets/multi\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/rewards/get-multiple-markets-with-rewards\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"Get earnings for user by date\",\"description\":\"Returns an array of user earnings per market for a provided day.\\n\\nRequires CLOB L2 Auth headers.\\n\\nResults are paginated (100 items per page). Use next_cursor to fetch subsequent pages.\\nA next_cursor value of \\\"LTE=\\\" indicates the last page.\\n\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"openapi\":\"/api-spec/clob-openapi.yaml get /rewards/user\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/rewards/get-earnings-for-user-by-date\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"Get total earnings for user by date\",\"description\":\"Returns the summed total rewards earnings for a user on a provided day,\\ngrouped by asset address.\\n\\nRequires CLOB L2 Auth headers.\\n\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"openapi\":\"/api-spec/clob-openapi.yaml get /rewards/user/total\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/rewards/get-total-earnings-for-user-by-date\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"Get reward percentages for user\",\"description\":\"Returns the real-time percentages of rewards that a user is earning per market.\\n\\nThe response is a map of condition_id to the percentage of total rewards\\nthe user is currently earning in that market.\\n\\nRequires CLOB L2 Auth headers.\\n\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"openapi\":\"/api-spec/clob-openapi.yaml get /rewards/user/percentages\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/rewards/get-reward-percentages-for-user\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"Get user earnings and markets configuration\",\"description\":\"Returns an array of current rewards including user earnings and live percentages\\nper market for a provided day.\\n\\nResults are paginated (100 items per page by default, max 500). Use next_cursor to fetch subsequent pages.\\nA next_cursor value of \\\"LTE=\\\" indicates the last page.\\n\\nRequires CLOB L2 Auth headers.\\n\\nOptional features:\\n- Search by question/description using the `q` parameter\\n- Filter by tag slugs using `tag_slug` parameter (multiple values are OR'ed)\\n- Filter by favorite markets using `favorite_markets=true`\\n- Sort by various fields using `order_by` and `position` parameters\\n\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"openapi\":\"/api-spec/clob-openapi.yaml get /rewards/user/markets\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/rewards/get-user-earnings-and-markets-configuration\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true}]},{\"group\":\"Profile\",\"pages\":[{\"title\":\"Get public profile by wallet address\",\"description\":null,\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"openapi\":\"/api-spec/gamma-openapi.yaml get /public-profile\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/profiles/get-public-profile-by-wallet-address\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"Get a user's profile stats\",\"description\":\"$4b\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"openapi\":\"https:/data-api.polymarket.com/v2/openapi.json get /v2/user-stats\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/wallet/get-a-users-profile-stats\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"List positions for a user or market\",\"description\":\"$4c\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"openapi\":\"https:/data-api.polymarket.com/v2/openapi.json get /v2/positions\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/wallet/list-positions-for-a-user-or-market\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"Get portfolio value\",\"description\":\"The user's portfolio value: single-market holdings marked to market plus\\nunresolved combo positions at cost basis.\\n\\n`?user=` is required (400 otherwise). `?condition=` (CSV of `condition_id`)\\nscopes the single-market term, and any condition filter excludes the\\nportfolio-level combo term. `data` is a single object; a user\\nwith no positions yields `{ \\\"data\\\": { \\\"proxy_wallet\\\": …, \\\"value\\\": 0 } }`.\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"openapi\":\"https:/data-api.polymarket.com/v2/openapi.json get /v2/value\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/wallet/get-portfolio-value\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"Get a user's PnL series\",\"description\":\"Complete cumulative native-PnL atoms and compositions.\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"openapi\":\"https:/data-api.polymarket.com/v2/openapi.json get /v2/user-pnl\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/wallet/get-a-users-pnl-series\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"Get a user's trading volume\",\"description\":\"One wallet's trading volume over a window, in both\\nunits side by side.\\n\\n`?user=` is required. `?start=` / `?end=` are epoch seconds, inclusive and\\noptional: omitted or `0` disables a bound (full history). Volume is tracked in\\nwhole UTC days, so each bound is floored to its UTC day; the served window\\nis the smallest whole-day window containing `[start, end]`.\\n\\nReturns `{ data: { volume, volume_usdc, trade_count } }`; exactly one row\\nby construction (the view aggregates with no GROUP BY), zeros for a wallet\\nwith no trades in the window. An inverted window is zeros too, not an error.\\n\\n`volume` is both-sides SHARES; `volume_usdc` is the same measure in USD;\\nthe endpoint that shows the unit convention side by side: the bare name is\\nthe natural unit, `_usdc` is the denomination, the same pairing as\\n`current_size` / `entry_cost_usdc` on `/v2/positions`.\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"openapi\":\"https:/data-api.polymarket.com/v2/openapi.json get /v2/user-volume\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/wallet/get-a-users-trading-volume\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"List account activity\",\"description\":\"Keyset-paginated activity feed (trades, splits, merges,\\nredeems, …) in the standard `{ data, pagination }` envelope.\\n\\nOrdering is `(block_timestamp, sequence_id)`, `DESC` by default or `ASC` via\\n`sort_direction=ASC`; both keyset-seekable. Value sorts (`CASH`/`TOKENS`)\\nhave no seek anchor and are rejected with `400` rather than silently\\nre-served as page one. The cursor binds the direction it was minted under\\nand the resume ADOPTS it, so a replay cannot flip the walk mid-stream.\\n\\nA malformed `condition` id is a `400` naming the value; a\\nwell-formed one that matches nothing serves an empty `data` array, which\\nis the meaningful zero-state; absence means the market is not servable,\\nand only that.\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"openapi\":\"https:/data-api.polymarket.com/v2/openapi.json get /v2/activity\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/feeds/list-account-activity\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"Get wallet approvals\",\"description\":\"Polygon token/operator approval state for one wallet.\\n\\n`?user=` must be an EVM address. The complete served catalog is returned in\\ncanonical order under `{ data }`; this endpoint is not paginated.\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"openapi\":\"https:/data-api.polymarket.com/v2/openapi.json get /v2/approvals\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/wallet/get-wallet-approvals\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true}]},{\"group\":\"Boards\",\"pages\":[{\"title\":\"Get the trader leaderboard\",\"description\":\"$4d\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"openapi\":\"https://data-api.polymarket.com/v2/openapi.json get /v2/leaderboard\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/boards/get-the-trader-leaderboard\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"List the biggest wins\",\"description\":\"The biggest single winning positions.\\n\\nOne row per winning POSITION, not per user: `pnl` is\\n`final_value - initial_value` for that position, and the window\\n(`?time_period=`, default `day`) is on when it resolved. `?category=`\\nnarrows to a market category. Deeper pages come only from `?cursor=`,\\nwhich **pins the window and category it was minted on**; restating a\\ndifferent one is a `400`, not a silent re-point.\\n\\nCombo wins are first-class rows here, tagged `kind = \\\"combo\\\"`. They carry a\\n`' / '`-joined title of their legs and no Gamma event; `event_id` is `0`\\nand `event_slug` empty; so **branch on `kind` before building an event\\nlink**.\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"openapi\":\"https://data-api.polymarket.com/v2/openapi.json get /v2/biggest-winners\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/boards/list-the-biggest-wins\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"Get the builders leaderboard\",\"description\":\"The ranked board of builders by volume.\\n\\n`?time_period=` is `day` (default), `week`, `month` or `all` and selects the\\n**window**; one row per builder in it. Deeper pages come only from\\n`?cursor=`.\\n\\nA cursor **pins the window it was minted on**, so following it needs no\\n`?time_period=`; and passing a different one is a `400` rather than a\\nsilent re-point, since an offset from one board means nothing on another.\\n\\n`volume` is in SHARES, not USDC, the same unit as `/v2/leaderboard`'s\\n`volume`. `active_users` counts distinct makers in the window.\\n\\n`builder` is a display name that falls back to `builder_code` for a builder\\nwith no profile, so key on `builder_code` and render `builder`.\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"openapi\":\"https://data-api.polymarket.com/v2/openapi.json get /v2/builders/leaderboard\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/boards/get-the-builders-leaderboard\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"Get builder volume over time\",\"description\":\"The per-builder volume time series.\\n\\n`?interval=` is the **bucket width**, not a window: `day` (default) returns\\nevery day on record bucketed daily, `week` and `month` bucket accordingly,\\nand `all` buckets by calendar YEAR. `?limit=` bounds how many of the most\\nrecent buckets come back (default 30); buckets, not rows, so a period is\\nnever returned half-populated. `timePeriod` is accepted as an alias for\\n`interval`.\\n\\n`rank` is the builder's placing **within its own bucket**, so it moves along\\nthe series. `volume` is in SHARES; see `/v2/builders/leaderboard`.\\n\\nNot paginated: `data` is the array with no `pagination`, the `/v2/oi` shape.\\nRows arrive newest bucket first, ranked within each.\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"openapi\":\"https://data-api.polymarket.com/v2/openapi.json get /v2/builders/volume\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/boards/get-builder-volume-over-time\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true}]},{\"group\":\"Search\",\"pages\":[{\"title\":\"Search markets, events, and profiles\",\"description\":null,\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"openapi\":\"/api-spec/gamma-openapi.yaml get /public-search\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/search/search-markets-events-and-profiles\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true}]},{\"group\":\"Tags\",\"pages\":[{\"title\":\"List tags\",\"description\":null,\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"openapi\":\"/api-spec/gamma-openapi.yaml get /tags\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/tags/list-tags\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"Get tag by id\",\"description\":null,\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"openapi\":\"/api-spec/gamma-openapi.yaml get /tags/{id}\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/tags/get-tag-by-id\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"Get tag by slug\",\"description\":null,\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"openapi\":\"/api-spec/gamma-openapi.yaml get /tags/slug/{slug}\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/tags/get-tag-by-slug\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"Get related tags (relationships) by tag id\",\"description\":null,\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"openapi\":\"/api-spec/gamma-openapi.yaml get /tags/{id}/related-tags\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/tags/get-related-tags-relationships-by-tag-id\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"Get related tags (relationships) by tag slug\",\"description\":null,\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"openapi\":\"/api-spec/gamma-openapi.yaml get /tags/slug/{slug}/related-tags\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/tags/get-related-tags-relationships-by-tag-slug\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"Get tags related to a tag id\",\"description\":null,\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"openapi\":\"/api-spec/gamma-openapi.yaml get /tags/{id}/related-tags/tags\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/tags/get-tags-related-to-a-tag-id\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"Get tags related to a tag slug\",\"description\":null,\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"openapi\":\"/api-spec/gamma-openapi.yaml get /tags/slug/{slug}/related-tags/tags\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/tags/get-tags-related-to-a-tag-slug\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true}]},{\"group\":\"Series\",\"pages\":[{\"title\":\"List series\",\"description\":null,\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"openapi\":\"/api-spec/gamma-openapi.yaml get /series\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/series/list-series\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"Get series by id\",\"description\":null,\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"openapi\":\"/api-spec/gamma-openapi.yaml get /series/{id}\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/series/get-series-by-id\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true}]},{\"group\":\"Comments\",\"pages\":[{\"title\":\"List comments\",\"description\":null,\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"openapi\":\"/api-spec/gamma-openapi.yaml get /comments\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/comments/list-comments\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"Get comments by comment id\",\"description\":null,\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"openapi\":\"/api-spec/gamma-openapi.yaml get /comments/{id}\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/comments/get-comments-by-comment-id\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"Get comments by user address\",\"description\":null,\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"openapi\":\"/api-spec/gamma-openapi.yaml get /comments/user_address/{user_address}\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/comments/get-comments-by-user-address\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true}]},{\"group\":\"Sports\",\"pages\":[{\"title\":\"Get sports metadata information\",\"description\":null,\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"openapi\":\"/api-spec/gamma-openapi.yaml get /sports\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/sports/get-sports-metadata-information\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"Get valid sports market types\",\"description\":null,\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"openapi\":\"/api-spec/gamma-openapi.yaml get /sports/market-types\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/sports/get-valid-sports-market-types\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"List teams\",\"description\":null,\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"openapi\":\"/api-spec/gamma-openapi.yaml get /teams\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/sports/list-teams\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true}]},{\"group\":\"Relayer\",\"pages\":[{\"title\":\"Submit a transaction\",\"description\":\"Submit a transaction request to the Relayer. Authenticated using Builder API Keys or Relayer API Keys.\\n\\nReturns immediately with the `transactionID` and a `state` of `STATE_NEW`. The onchain transaction hash is **not** included in this response — poll `GET /transaction` with the returned `transactionID` to retrieve the `transactionHash` once the transaction has been broadcast.\\n\\n**Builder API Key auth headers:**\\n- `POLY_BUILDER_API_KEY`\\n- `POLY_BUILDER_TIMESTAMP`\\n- `POLY_BUILDER_PASSPHRASE`\\n- `POLY_BUILDER_SIGNATURE`\\n\\n**Relayer API Key auth headers:**\\n- `RELAYER_API_KEY`\\n- `RELAYER_API_KEY_ADDRESS`\\n\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"openapi\":\"/api-spec/relayer-openapi.yaml post /submit\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/relayer/submit-a-transaction\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"Get a transaction by ID\",\"description\":\"Gets a transaction submitted to the Relayer. Takes in a required transaction ID as a query parameter.\\n\\nPoll this endpoint with the `transactionID` returned from `POST /submit` to retrieve the onchain `transactionHash` once the transaction has been broadcast.\\n\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"openapi\":\"/api-spec/relayer-openapi.yaml get /transaction\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/relayer/get-a-transaction-by-id\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"Get recent transactions for a user\",\"description\":\"Gets the most recent transactions submitted to the Relayer, owned by a specific user. Authenticated using Builder API Keys or Relayer API Keys.\\n\\n**Builder API Key auth headers:**\\n- `POLY_BUILDER_API_KEY`\\n- `POLY_BUILDER_TIMESTAMP`\\n- `POLY_BUILDER_PASSPHRASE`\\n- `POLY_BUILDER_SIGNATURE`\\n\\n**Relayer API Key auth headers:**\\n- `RELAYER_API_KEY`\\n- `RELAYER_API_KEY_ADDRESS`\\n\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"openapi\":\"/api-spec/relayer-openapi.yaml get /transactions\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/relayer/get-recent-transactions-for-a-user\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"Get current nonce for a user\",\"description\":\"Gets the current Proxy or Safe nonce for a user. Takes in the user's signer address and the type of nonce to retrieve.\\n\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"openapi\":\"/api-spec/relayer-openapi.yaml get /nonce\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/relayer/get-current-nonce-for-a-user\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"Get relayer address and nonce\",\"description\":\"Fetches the relayer address and nonce for a specific user. Takes in the user's signer address and the type of nonce to retrieve.\\n\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"openapi\":\"/api-spec/relayer-openapi.yaml get /relay-payload\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/relayer/get-relayer-address-and-nonce\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"Check if a wallet is deployed\",\"description\":\"Returns whether the wallet at the given address is deployed onchain.\\n\\nUse the `type` query parameter to choose which wallet type to check:\\n\\n- Pass user's Polymarket `SAFE` address (default): Gnosis Safe (SignatureType `2`).\\n- Pass user's Polymarket `WALLET` Deposit Wallet address: Deposit Wallet (signatureType `3`). See the [Deposit Wallet Guide](/trading/deposit-wallets) for setup.\\n\\nOmitting `type` is equivalent to `type=SAFE`.\\n\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"openapi\":\"/api-spec/relayer-openapi.yaml get /deployed\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/relayer/check-if-a-wallet-is-deployed\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"Get all relayer API keys\",\"description\":\"Returns all relayer API keys for the authenticated address. Auth allowed: Gamma auth or Relayer API key auth (`RELAYER_API_KEY` + `RELAYER_API_KEY_ADDRESS`).\\n\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"openapi\":\"/api-spec/relayer-openapi.yaml get /relayer/api/keys\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/relayer-api-keys/get-all-relayer-api-keys\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true}]},{\"group\":\"Combos\",\"tag\":\"New\",\"pages\":[{\"title\":\"Get combo markets\",\"description\":\"Returns active markets that can be used as combo legs, ordered by volume\\ndescending. This endpoint is public and does not require CLOB\\nauthentication.\\n\\nEntries in `position_ids`, `outcomes`, and `outcome_prices` correspond by\\narray index (`[0]` is YES, `[1]` is NO). Use `next_cursor` unchanged in\\nthe next request; a value of `null` indicates the final page.\\n\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"openapi\":\"/api-spec/combos-rfq-openapi.yaml get /v1/rfq/combo-markets\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/combo-markets/get-combo-markets\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"Submit a quote\",\"description\":\"Submit a signed maker quote for an active RFQ. Requires CLOB L2\\nauthentication for the maker role.\\n\\nREST does not assign a quote ID — generate `quote_id` client-side.\\n\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"openapi\":\"/api-spec/combos-rfq-openapi.yaml post /v1/maker/quotes\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/maker/submit-a-quote\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"Cancel a quote\",\"description\":\"Cancel an active maker quote before it is selected. Requires CLOB L2\\nauthentication for the maker role. `signer_address` and `maker_address`\\nmust match the authenticated identity.\\n\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"openapi\":\"/api-spec/combos-rfq-openapi.yaml post /v1/maker/quotes/cancel\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/maker/cancel-a-quote\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"Confirm or decline last look\",\"description\":\"Respond to a last-look confirmation request for a selected quote. Requires\\nCLOB L2 authentication for the maker role. `decision` must be `CONFIRM` or\\n`DECLINE`.\\n\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"openapi\":\"/api-spec/combos-rfq-openapi.yaml post /v1/maker/confirmations\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/maker/confirm-or-decline-last-look\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"List combo positions\",\"description\":\"$4e\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"openapi\":\"https:/data-api.polymarket.com/v2/openapi.json get /v2/positions/combos\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/wallet/list-combo-positions\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"List combo activity\",\"description\":\"Keyset-paginated combo lifecycle + redemption\\nfeed for a user, in the standard `{ data, pagination }` envelope.\\n\\nPass `?cursor=` from a prior response's `next_cursor` to fetch the next page.\\nUnlike the activity feed, the anchor behind the cursor is\\n`(block_number, log_index)`; this endpoint's total order.\\n\\nA malformed `condition` combo condition id is a `400` naming the value; a\\nwell-formed one that matches nothing serves an empty `data` array, which\\nis the meaningful zero-state.\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"openapi\":\"https:/data-api.polymarket.com/v2/openapi.json get /v2/activity/combos\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/feeds/list-combo-activity\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"Quoter Gateway\",\"description\":\"Authenticated WebSocket for combinatorial RFQ quoters — receive requests, submit quotes, confirm last look, and track execution.\",\"asyncapi\":\"asyncapi-rfq.json quoter\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/wss/rfq\"}]},{\"group\":\"WebSocket\",\"pages\":[{\"title\":\"Market Channel\",\"description\":\"Public WebSocket for real-time orderbook, price, and market lifecycle updates.\",\"asyncapi\":\"asyncapi.json market\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/wss/market\"},{\"title\":\"User Channel\",\"description\":\"Authenticated WebSocket for real-time order and trade updates.\",\"asyncapi\":\"asyncapi-user.json user\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/wss/user\"},{\"title\":\"Sports Channel\",\"description\":\"Public WebSocket for real-time sports match results.\",\"asyncapi\":\"asyncapi-sports.json sports\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/wss/sports\"}]},{\"group\":\"PolyBolt WebSocket\",\"tag\":\"New\",\"pages\":[{\"title\":\"PolyBolt WebSocket\",\"description\":\"Stream crypto, equity and TWAP reference prices over one WebSocket connection.\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/live-data/overview\"},{\"title\":\"Live Data Channel\",\"description\":\"PolyBolt WebSocket message reference for crypto, equity and TWAP reference prices.\",\"asyncapi\":\"https://ws-live-v2.polymarket.com/asyncapi.json ws\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/wss/polybolt\"},{\"group\":\"Websockets\",\"pages\":[{\"asyncapi\":\"https://ws-live-v2.polymarket.com/asyncapi.json ws\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/websockets/live-data-channel\",\"title\":\"Live Data Channel\",\"description\":\"Send JSON text frames tagged with op. The server answers every op with an ack or an error ack (never a close, except for policy breaches, close 4008) and pushes envelopes for subscribed channels. Limits per connection: 64 active (channel, filter) subscriptions, 20 subscribe or unsubscribe frames per second (a batch frame counts once), 64 KB per frame, 8 auth attempts. The server sends a WebSocket ping every 25 seconds; two missed pongs close 4002. Close codes: 4001 authentication failed on a presented credential, 4002 slow consumer or pong timeout, 4003 server draining (reconnect once after a uniform 0 to 10 s delay), 4008 policy violation (fix the client; do not reconnect blindly).\",\"version\":null,\"autogeneratedByAsyncApi\":true}]}]},{\"group\":\"Bridge\",\"pages\":[{\"title\":\"Get supported assets\",\"description\":null,\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"openapi\":\"/api-spec/bridge-openapi.yaml get /supported-assets\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/bridge/get-supported-assets\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"Create bridge addresses\",\"description\":null,\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"openapi\":\"/api-spec/bridge-openapi.yaml post /deposit\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/bridge/create-bridge-addresses\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"Get a quote\",\"description\":null,\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"openapi\":\"/api-spec/bridge-openapi.yaml post /quote\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/bridge/get-a-quote\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"Get transaction status\",\"description\":\"Returns the deposits and withdrawals seen at a bridge address, newest first. Responses are cursor-paginated: each request returns one page plus a `nextCursor`. To read the full history, pass each `nextCursor` back as `cursor` until it comes back null. To track only recent activity, keep requesting the first page without a cursor.\\n\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"openapi\":\"/api-spec/bridge-openapi.yaml get /status/{address}\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/bridge/get-transaction-status\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"Create withdrawal addresses\",\"description\":null,\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"openapi\":\"/api-spec/bridge-openapi.yaml post /withdraw\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/bridge/create-withdrawal-addresses\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true}]},{\"group\":\"Data API v1 (Legacy)\",\"pages\":[{\"title\":\"Get current positions for a user\",\"description\":\"**Data API v2:** this route has a v2 counterpart, `GET /v2/positions`. See [Migrating to Data API v2](/migrate/data-api-v1-to-v2).\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"openapi\":\"/api-spec/data-openapi.yaml get /positions\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/core/get-current-positions-for-a-user\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"Get closed positions for a user\",\"description\":\"**Data API v2:** this route has a v2 counterpart, `GET /v2/positions?status=CLOSED`. See [Migrating to Data API v2](/migrate/data-api-v1-to-v2).\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"openapi\":\"/api-spec/data-openapi.yaml get /closed-positions\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/core/get-closed-positions-for-a-user\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"Get positions for a market\",\"description\":\"**Data API v2:** this route has a v2 counterpart, `GET /v2/positions`. See [Migrating to Data API v2](/migrate/data-api-v1-to-v2).\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"openapi\":\"/api-spec/data-openapi.yaml get /v1/market-positions\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/core/get-positions-for-a-market\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"Get trades for a user or markets\",\"description\":\"**Data API v2:** this route has a v2 counterpart, `GET /v2/trades`. See [Migrating to Data API v2](/migrate/data-api-v1-to-v2).\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"openapi\":\"/api-spec/data-openapi.yaml get /trades\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/core/get-trades-for-a-user-or-markets\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"Get user activity\",\"description\":\"**Data API v2:** this route has a v2 counterpart, `GET /v2/activity`. See [Migrating to Data API v2](/migrate/data-api-v1-to-v2).\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"openapi\":\"/api-spec/data-openapi.yaml get /activity\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/core/get-user-activity\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"Get total value of a user's positions\",\"description\":\"**Data API v2:** this route has a v2 counterpart, `GET /v2/value`. See [Migrating to Data API v2](/migrate/data-api-v1-to-v2).\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"openapi\":\"/api-spec/data-openapi.yaml get /value\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/core/get-total-value-of-a-users-positions\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"Get total markets a user has traded\",\"description\":null,\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"openapi\":\"/api-spec/data-openapi.yaml get /traded\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/misc/get-total-markets-a-user-has-traded\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"Download an accounting snapshot (ZIP of CSVs)\",\"description\":null,\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"openapi\":\"/api-spec/data-openapi.yaml get /v1/accounting/snapshot\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/misc/download-an-accounting-snapshot-zip-of-csvs\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"Get top holders for markets\",\"description\":\"**Data API v2:** this route has a v2 counterpart, `GET /v2/holders`. See [Migrating to Data API v2](/migrate/data-api-v1-to-v2).\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"openapi\":\"/api-spec/data-openapi.yaml get /holders\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/core/get-top-holders-for-markets\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"Get open interest\",\"description\":\"**Data API v2:** this route has a v2 counterpart, `GET /v2/oi`. See [Migrating to Data API v2](/migrate/data-api-v1-to-v2).\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"openapi\":\"/api-spec/data-openapi.yaml get /oi\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/misc/get-open-interest\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"Get live volume for an event\",\"description\":\"**Data API v2:** this route has a v2 counterpart, `GET /v2/live-volume`. See [Migrating to Data API v2](/migrate/data-api-v1-to-v2).\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"openapi\":\"/api-spec/data-openapi.yaml get /live-volume\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/misc/get-live-volume-for-an-event\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"Get trader leaderboard rankings\",\"description\":\"**Data API v2:** this route has a v2 counterpart, `GET /v2/leaderboard`. See [Migrating to Data API v2](/migrate/data-api-v1-to-v2).\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"openapi\":\"/api-spec/data-openapi.yaml get /v1/leaderboard\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/core/get-trader-leaderboard-rankings\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"Get aggregated builder leaderboard\",\"description\":\"**Data API v2:** this route has a v2 counterpart, `GET /v2/builders/leaderboard`. See [Migrating to Data API v2](/migrate/data-api-v1-to-v2).\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"openapi\":\"/api-spec/data-openapi.yaml get /v1/builders/leaderboard\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/builders/get-aggregated-builder-leaderboard\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"Get daily builder volume time-series\",\"description\":\"**Data API v2:** this route has a v2 counterpart, `GET /v2/builders/volume`. See [Migrating to Data API v2](/migrate/data-api-v1-to-v2).\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"openapi\":\"/api-spec/data-openapi.yaml get /v1/builders/volume\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/builders/get-daily-builder-volume-time-series\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"Get user combo positions\",\"description\":\"**Data API v2:** this route has a v2 counterpart, `GET /v2/positions/combos`. See [Migrating to Data API v2](/migrate/data-api-v1-to-v2).\\nCombinatorial (multi-market) positions held by a user, with per-leg breakdown. Also available at /v1/data/user/{address}/positions/combos (address from the path). Open positions with shares_balance below 0.001 are omitted (dust floor — e.g. sub-0.001 remainders left by \\\"sell all\\\" cashouts); resolved positions are served regardless of balance.\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"openapi\":\"/api-spec/data-openapi.yaml get /v1/positions/combos\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/core/get-user-combo-positions\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"Get user combo activity\",\"description\":\"**Data API v2:** this route has a v2 counterpart, `GET /v2/activity/combos`. See [Migrating to Data API v2](/migrate/data-api-v1-to-v2).\\nCombo lifecycle and redeem events (split / merge / convert / compress / wrap / unwrap / redeem) for a user, with per-leg breakdown. The combo counterpart to /activity trade rows. Also available at /v1/data/user/{address}/activity/combos (address from the path).\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"openapi\":\"/api-spec/data-openapi.yaml get /v1/activity/combos\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/core/get-user-combo-activity\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true}]},{\"title\":\"Data API v2\",\"description\":\"Read wallet portfolios, trade and activity feeds, market state, and ranked leaderboards through one consistent response contract.\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/data-api/overview\"}]},{\"dropdown\":\"Perps\",\"icon\":\"chart-line\",\"pages\":[{\"title\":\"Overview\",\"description\":\"Explore the APIs available for building with Polymarket Perps.\",\"hideFooterPagination\":true,\"href\":\"/api-reference/perps/overview\"},{\"title\":\"Rate Limits\",\"description\":\"IP rate limits, action rate limits, and WebSocket limits for Perps integrations\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/perps/rate-limits\"},{\"title\":\"Geographic Restrictions\",\"description\":\"Jurisdictions where Polymarket Perps order placement is not permitted\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/perps/geographic-restrictions\"},{\"group\":\"HTTP\",\"pages\":[{\"title\":\"Test Connection\",\"description\":\"Test connection to the server.\\n\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"openapi\":\"/api-spec/perps-openapi.json get /v1/info/ping\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/test-connection\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"Get Server Time\",\"description\":\"Get server time.\\n\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"openapi\":\"/api-spec/perps-openapi.json get /v1/info/time\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/get-server-time\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"Get Exchange Info\",\"description\":\"Get exchange information.\\n\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"openapi\":\"/api-spec/perps-openapi.json get /v1/info/exchange\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/get-exchange-info\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"Get Collateral Assets\",\"description\":\"Get a list of collateral assets.\\n\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"openapi\":\"/api-spec/perps-openapi.json get /v1/info/assets\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/get-collateral-assets\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"Get Instruments\",\"description\":\"Get all instruments.\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"openapi\":\"/api-spec/perps-openapi.json get /v1/info/instruments\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/get-instruments\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"Get Tickers\",\"description\":\"Get all instrument tickers with live market data.\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"openapi\":\"/api-spec/perps-openapi.json get /v1/info/tickers\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/get-tickers\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"Get Statistics\",\"description\":\"Get last 24-hour statistics for all instruments.\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"openapi\":\"/api-spec/perps-openapi.json get /v1/info/statistics\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/get-statistics\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"Get Exchange Statistics\",\"description\":\"Get aggregate statistics for all pUSD-quoted Polymarket perpetual markets.\\nThe time window is half-open: trades at `start_timestamp` are included and trades at\\n`end_timestamp` are excluded. The maximum window is 31 days.\\nOpen interest is the one-sided USD notional from the latest complete sample before\\n`end_timestamp`; its value and timestamp are null when no complete sample is available.\\nFees are gross positive maker and taker trading fees. Rebates, incentives, and referral\\npayments are excluded.\\n\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"openapi\":\"/api-spec/perps-openapi.json get /v1/info/exchange-stats\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/get-exchange-statistics\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"Get Leaderboard\",\"description\":\"$4f\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"openapi\":\"/api-spec/perps-openapi.json get /v1/info/leaderboard\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/get-leaderboard\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"Get Klines\",\"description\":\"Get klines for an instrument.\\nIf no end time is provided, the current time will be used.\\nMaximum of 1000 entries returned per request.\\n\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"openapi\":\"/api-spec/perps-openapi.json get /v1/info/klines\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/get-klines\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"Get Mark Price History\",\"description\":\"Get mark price history for an instrument, bucketed by interval.\\nIf no end time is provided, the current time will be used.\\nMaximum of 1000 entries returned per request.\\nOnly buckets with at least one mark update are included.\\nFor intervals of a minute or coarser, a bucket cut mid-way by `end_timestamp`\\nmay be omitted, or may reflect the window's last mark at one-minute fidelity.\\n\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"openapi\":\"/api-spec/perps-openapi.json get /v1/info/mark-history\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/get-mark-price-history\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"Get BBO\",\"description\":\"Get best bid and offer for all instruments.\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"openapi\":\"/api-spec/perps-openapi.json get /v1/info/bbo\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/get-bbo\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"Get Book\",\"description\":\"Get book for an instrument.\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"openapi\":\"/api-spec/perps-openapi.json get /v1/info/book\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/get-book\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"Get Index\",\"description\":\"Get index price and the list of constituents for an asset.\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"openapi\":\"/api-spec/perps-openapi.json get /v1/info/index\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/get-index\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"Get Recent Trades\",\"description\":\"Get public trades for an instrument.\\nMaximum of 100 entries returned per request.\\n\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"openapi\":\"/api-spec/perps-openapi.json get /v1/info/trades\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/get-recent-trades\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"Get Public Portfolio\",\"description\":\"Get public portfolio for an address including equity and open positions.\\n\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"openapi\":\"/api-spec/perps-openapi.json get /v1/info/portfolio\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/get-public-portfolio\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"Get Current Position Fills\",\"description\":\"$50\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"openapi\":\"/api-spec/perps-openapi.json get /v1/info/position-fills\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/get-current-position-fills\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"Get Historical Funding\",\"description\":\"Get public funding rate history for an instrument.\\nMaximum of 100 entries returned per request.\\n\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"openapi\":\"/api-spec/perps-openapi.json get /v1/info/funding\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/get-historical-funding\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"Get Fees\",\"description\":\"Get the fee tier schedule for each instrument type and category.\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"openapi\":\"/api-spec/perps-openapi.json get /v1/info/fees\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/get-fees\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"Get Limit Tiers\",\"description\":\"Get the list of account limit tiers. Action and open-order fields are enforced per account; legacy request-rate fields are not used for gateway request enforcement.\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"openapi\":\"/api-spec/perps-openapi.json get /v1/info/limit-tiers\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/get-limit-tiers\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"Check Invite Code\",\"description\":\"Check whether an invite code can be used. When `address` is provided, the\\nresponse is invalid if that address already has an account.\\n\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"openapi\":\"/api-spec/perps-openapi.json get /v1/info/invite\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/check-invite-code\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"Create Orders\",\"description\":\"Create new orders.\\nRequires proxy signature, see [proxy signing](/http/signing#2-proxy-signing).\\n\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"openapi\":\"/api-spec/perps-openapi.json post /v1/trade/orders\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/create-orders\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"Modify Orders\",\"description\":\"Modify the price and total quantity of existing orders by exchange order ID.\\nRequires proxy signature, see [proxy signing](/http/signing#2-proxy-signing).\\n\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"openapi\":\"/api-spec/perps-openapi.json patch /v1/trade/orders\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/modify-orders\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"Modify Orders COID\",\"description\":\"Modify the price and total quantity of existing orders by client order ID.\\nRequires proxy signature, see [proxy signing](/http/signing#2-proxy-signing).\\n\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"openapi\":\"/api-spec/perps-openapi.json patch /v1/trade/orders-coid\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/modify-orders-coid\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"Cancel Orders\",\"description\":\"Cancel orders.\\nRequires proxy signature, see [proxy signing](/http/signing#2-proxy-signing).\\n\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"openapi\":\"/api-spec/perps-openapi.json delete /v1/trade/orders\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/cancel-orders\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"Cancel Orders COID\",\"description\":\"Cancel orders by client order ID.\\nRequires proxy signature, see [proxy signing](/http/signing#2-proxy-signing).\\n\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"openapi\":\"/api-spec/perps-openapi.json delete /v1/trade/orders-coid\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/cancel-orders-coid\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"Cancel All Orders\",\"description\":\"Cancel all open orders for the authenticated account on one instrument.\\nRequires proxy signature, see [proxy signing](/http/signing#2-proxy-signing).\\n\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"openapi\":\"/api-spec/perps-openapi.json delete /v1/trade/orders/all\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/cancel-all-orders\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"Set Auto-Cancel\",\"description\":\"Set a dead man's switch that cancels all your open orders at the chosen\\ntime. The time must be at least 5 seconds in the future. Send 0 to clear\\nan active schedule without triggering it; posting a new time replaces the\\ncurrent one.\\n\\nThe switch fires once, then clears itself. It does not cover orders you\\nplace after it fires, so re-arm it if you still need protection.\\n\\nAn account can trigger auto-cancel up to 1000 times per UTC day. After\\nthat, the API rejects new schedules with the error\\n`auto_cancel_daily_limit_reached` until the next UTC day. Clearing a\\nschedule is always allowed. To check the active deadline and today's\\ntrigger count, call [Get Auto-Cancel Status](/api-reference/get-auto-cancel-status).\\n\\nRequires proxy signature, see [proxy signing](/http/signing#2-proxy-signing).\\n\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"openapi\":\"/api-spec/perps-openapi.json patch /v1/trade/auto-cancel\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/set-auto-cancel\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"Update Leverage\",\"description\":\"$51\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"openapi\":\"/api-spec/perps-openapi.json patch /v1/trade/leverage\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/update-leverage\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"Update Leverage for Multiple Instruments\",\"description\":\"$52\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"openapi\":\"/api-spec/perps-openapi.json patch /v1/trade/leverage/batch\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/update-leverage-for-multiple-instruments\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"Update Isolated Margin\",\"description\":\"Adjust the signed collateral allocation for an existing isolated position.\\nUse a positive amount to add margin and a negative amount to remove it.\\nA removal may include unrealized isolated profit, but the resulting\\nisolated position equity (allocation + unrealized PnL - settled funding)\\nmust remain at or above the position's current required initial margin.\\n\\nBoth additions and removals are rejected while the account is in cross\\nliquidation or the target isolated position is in isolated liquidation.\\nAn isolated liquidation on another instrument does not block this request.\\n\\nCancel-only mode does not gate margin adjustments.\\n\\nRequires proxy signature, see [proxy signing](/http/signing#2-proxy-signing).\\nGateway signature validation rejects a stale or future-skewed timestamp as\\n`invalid signature`. A request that passes gateway validation can still fail\\nsequencer freshness revalidation with\\n`invalid_margin_signature_timestamp`. Reusing the exact signed request\\nrejects with `signature_already_used`.\\n\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"openapi\":\"/api-spec/perps-openapi.json patch /v1/trade/margin\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/update-isolated-margin\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"Create Proxy\",\"description\":\"Create a new proxy to sign orders. Returns an API secret for private account access.\\nRequires EOA signature, see [EOA signing](/http/signing#1-eoa-signing).\\n\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"openapi\":\"/api-spec/perps-openapi.json post /v1/account/proxy\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/create-proxy\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"Delete Proxy\",\"description\":\"Delete a proxy by address.\\nRequires EOA signature, see [EOA signing](/http/signing#1-eoa-signing).\\n\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"openapi\":\"/api-spec/perps-openapi.json delete /v1/account/proxy\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/delete-proxy\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"Get Credentials\",\"description\":\"Get the account ID, address, and proxy keys for the authenticated account.\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"openapi\":\"/api-spec/perps-openapi.json get /v1/account/credentials\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/get-credentials\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"Get Orders\",\"description\":\"Get historical order snapshots for the authenticated account from the order history database.\\nReturns the latest known state for each matching order, including accepted, open, partial,\\nfilled, and cancelled orders. For currently resting orders only, use Get Open Orders.\\nMaximum of 100 entries returned per request.\\n\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"openapi\":\"/api-spec/perps-openapi.json get /v1/account/orders\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/get-orders\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"Get Open Orders\",\"description\":\"Get open orders for the authenticated account.\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"openapi\":\"/api-spec/perps-openapi.json get /v1/account/open-orders\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/get-open-orders\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"Get Balances\",\"description\":\"Get asset balances for the authenticated account.\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"openapi\":\"/api-spec/perps-openapi.json get /v1/account/balances\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/get-balances\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"Get Portfolio\",\"description\":\"Get current portfolio snapshot including open positions, margin summary, and withdrawable balance.\\n\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"openapi\":\"/api-spec/perps-openapi.json get /v1/account/portfolio\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/get-portfolio\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"Get Fills\",\"description\":\"Get fill history for the authenticated account.\\nIf no end time is provided, the current time will be used.\\nMaximum of 100 entries returned per request.\\nResults are ordered by time; use `sort` to choose newest-first (`desc`,\\ndefault) or oldest-first (`asc`). To page through more than 100 fills,\\npass the `cursor` returned by the previous page (keep `sort` consistent\\nacross pages). Passing the trade ID of the last fill from the previous\\npage is also still accepted. Pass `instrument_id` to narrow the page to\\none instrument's fills; the window, cursor and sort apply unchanged.\\n\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"openapi\":\"/api-spec/perps-openapi.json get /v1/account/fills\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/get-fills\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"Get Equity\",\"description\":\"Get equity history for the authenticated account.\\nIf no end time is provided, the current time will be used.\\nEach point is the last equity sample in its `interval` bucket, stamped with\\nthat sample's own timestamp rather than the bucket's start — so every\\ntimestamp falls within the requested window. Buckets are aligned to the\\nUnix epoch.\\nEquity history is served at one-minute resolution, so `1s` is served as\\n`1m`.\\nMaximum of 1000 entries returned per request — of buckets, so a coarser\\ninterval covers a longer window before `more` is set. When `more` is true,\\npage by re-requesting from one millisecond past the last timestamp\\nreturned; that always lands on the next bucket, never back inside the one\\njust served.\\n\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"openapi\":\"/api-spec/perps-openapi.json get /v1/account/equity\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/get-equity\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"Get PnL\",\"description\":\"Get PnL history for the authenticated account.\\nIf no end time is provided, the current time will be used.\\nEach point is the PnL realized inside its `interval` bucket — not a running\\ntotal. Buckets are aligned to the Unix epoch, and one in which nothing was\\nrealized is omitted, so the series is sparse.\\nA point is stamped with the last populated hour in its bucket, not with the\\nbucket's start, so every returned timestamp falls within the requested\\nwindow. Window bounds select whole one-hour rollup rows before coarser\\nbuckets are formed.\\nMaximum of 1000 entries returned per request — of buckets, so a coarser\\ninterval covers a longer window before `more` is set. When `more` is true,\\npage by re-requesting from one millisecond past the last timestamp\\nreturned; that always lands on the next bucket, never back inside the one\\njust served.\\n\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"openapi\":\"/api-spec/perps-openapi.json get /v1/account/pnl\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/get-pnl\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"Get Account Backstop Transfers\",\"description\":\"Get exact quote cash transfers for backstops of the authenticated account.\\nDefaults to the last 90 days. Rows are ordered newest first.\\nIf no end time is provided, the current time will be used.\\nMaximum of 100 entries returned per request.\\n\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"openapi\":\"/api-spec/perps-openapi.json get /v1/account/backstops\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/get-account-backstop-transfers\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"Get Funding Charges\",\"description\":\"Get funding payment history for the authenticated account.\\nIf no end time is provided, the current time will be used.\\nMaximum of 100 entries returned per request.\\n\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"openapi\":\"/api-spec/perps-openapi.json get /v1/account/funding\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/get-funding-charges\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"Withdraw\",\"description\":\"Submit a signed withdrawal request.\\nRequires EOA signature, see [EOA signing](/http/signing#1-eoa-signing).\\n\\nThe `amount` field is the raw token amount including decimals (e.g. `\\\"100000000\\\"` for 100 USDC).\\nThis must match the `uint256 amount` value used in the EIP-712 `Withdraw` signature.\\n\\nThe `ts` field is Unix seconds (not milliseconds) because the on-chain contract validates it\\nagainst `block.timestamp`. It must also match the `uint64 ts` in the signed EIP-712 struct.\\n\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"openapi\":\"/api-spec/perps-openapi.json post /v1/account/withdraw\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/withdraw\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"Internal Transfer\",\"description\":\"Submit a signed internal ledger transfer between two exchange accounts.\\nSign with the source account owner or a non-expired trading key registered\\nto the source account. Trading-key signatures require both accounts to\\nbelong to the same nonzero, exchange-managed account group. Owner signatures\\nremain valid regardless of group membership.\\n\\nExpired trading keys receive `proxy_expired`; other authorization failures\\nreceive `signer_does_not_match_account`. An unknown destination receives 400\\n`destination account not found`.\\n\\nA 503 does not prove that the transfer was not submitted. Retry with backoff,\\nhonoring `Retry-After` when present, and resend the exact original signed\\nrequest. Do not create a fresh signature, salt, or timestamp for the retry: it\\nwould identify a separate transfer. A `signature_already_used` rejection does\\nnot confirm whether the original transfer completed.\\n\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"openapi\":\"/api-spec/perps-openapi.json post /v1/account/internal-transfer\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/internal-transfer\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"Get Deposits\",\"description\":\"Get deposit history for the authenticated account.\\nIf no end time is provided, the current time will be used.\\nMaximum of 100 entries returned per request.\\n\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"openapi\":\"/api-spec/perps-openapi.json get /v1/account/deposits\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/get-deposits\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"Get Internal Transfers\",\"description\":\"Get settled internal transfer history for the authenticated account.\\nReturns both inbound and outbound transfers unless `direction` narrows\\nthe page to one side; a value other than `in` or `out` is refused.\\n\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"openapi\":\"/api-spec/perps-openapi.json get /v1/account/internal-transfers\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/get-internal-transfers\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"Get Withdrawals\",\"description\":\"Get withdrawal history for the authenticated account.\\nIf no end time is provided, the current time will be used.\\nMaximum of 100 entries returned per request.\\n\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"openapi\":\"/api-spec/perps-openapi.json get /v1/account/withdrawals\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/get-withdrawals\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"Get Account Stats\",\"description\":\"Get the authenticated account's 7-day trading stats (taker volume, maker volume,\\naccount maker share, and entity maker share when applicable).\\nStats are cached by UTC day and may be stale by up to 24 hours.\\n\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"openapi\":\"/api-spec/perps-openapi.json get /v1/account/stats\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/get-account-stats\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"Get Account Limits\",\"description\":\"Get the authenticated account's effective rate-limit allowances for its current\\nvolume-based tier: order-action rate, open-order cap, and the display-only\\nmessages-per-minute figure. `open_orders` reflects the account's current live\\nopen-order count; the rate-usage counters (`actions_per_minute`,\\n`actions_burst`, and `reset`) are not tracked here and are reported as 0.\\n\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"openapi\":\"/api-spec/perps-openapi.json get /v1/account/limits\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/get-account-limits\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"Get Account Rewards\",\"description\":\"Get per-instrument daily liquidity reward shares for the authenticated account.\\nReward periods run from 12:00 UTC to 12:00 UTC and are labeled by their UTC end date.\\nOI rewards pay 6% APR on the account's full daily average gross OI across all\\ninstruments when the combined daily average gross OI of its rewards entity is\\nat least $5M. Accounts without an entity mapping qualify independently.\\nThe first reward period starts at 2026-07-06 12:00 UTC. If no date range is provided,\\nthe latest computed reward period is returned.\\n\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"openapi\":\"/api-spec/perps-openapi.json get /v1/account/rewards\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/get-account-rewards\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"Get Instrument Config\",\"description\":\"Get resolved per-instrument configuration (leverage and margin mode) for the authenticated account.\\nEach setting resolves independently: explicit per-instrument setting, then\\nexchange-managed account-group default, then instrument maximum leverage and\\nisolated margin. Group leverage is capped at the instrument maximum; a group\\ncross default resolves to isolated on isolated-only instruments. Group defaults\\napply to new listings and never overwrite explicit settings.\\nUse the leverage update operations to set explicit per-instrument overrides.\\n\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"openapi\":\"/api-spec/perps-openapi.json get /v1/account/config\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/get-instrument-config\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"Get Auto-Cancel Status\",\"description\":\"Get the current auto-cancel status for the authenticated account: the\\narmed deadline, how many times the switch has fired today, and when the\\ndaily counter resets.\\n\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"openapi\":\"/api-spec/perps-openapi.json get /v1/account/auto-cancel\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/get-auto-cancel-status\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"Create Account Invite\",\"description\":\"Create or return the authenticated account's primary invite code. The call\\nis idempotent for accounts that already have a primary invite code.\\n\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"openapi\":\"/api-spec/perps-openapi.json post /v1/account/invite\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/create-account-invite\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"Get Account Referral\",\"description\":\"Get the authenticated account's invite code, parent referral code, direct\\nreferral count, and fee share rate.\\n\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"openapi\":\"/api-spec/perps-openapi.json get /v1/account/referral\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/get-account-referral\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"Apply Referral Code\",\"description\":\"Apply a referral code to the authenticated account after signup. Accounts\\ncan only apply a referral code if they do not already have one.\\n\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"openapi\":\"/api-spec/perps-openapi.json post /v1/account/referral\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/apply-referral-code\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"Get Notifications\",\"description\":\"Get the authenticated account's notifications, newest first.\\n\\nResults come in pages. Pass the cursor returned by the previous page to\\nfetch the next, older one. If your WebSocket connection dropped or you\\nreceived a resync frame, pass since_seq to backfill anything you may have\\nmissed; the same notification can show up again at the edges of the\\nwindow, so deduplicate by id. While paging through a backfill, keep\\nsending the same since_seq with each cursor so every page stays inside\\nthe same window.\\n\\nThe response also includes your unread count and durable_source_seq, which\\ntells you how far the notification store has caught up. If a backfill has\\nnot yet reached your target sequence, wait briefly and retry with the same\\nsince_seq.\\n\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"openapi\":\"/api-spec/perps-openapi.json get /v1/account/notifications\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/get-notifications\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"Mark Notifications Read\",\"description\":\"Mark notifications as read. Send a list of notification ids, or a before\\ncursor to mark everything up to and including that point. You can only\\nmark your own notifications.\\n\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"openapi\":\"/api-spec/perps-openapi.json post /v1/account/notifications/read\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/mark-notifications-read\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true}]},{\"group\":\"WebSocket\",\"pages\":[{\"title\":\"Ping\",\"description\":\"Perps WebSocket heartbeat.\",\"asyncapi\":\"asyncapi-perps.json ping\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/wss/perps-ping\"},{\"title\":\"Place Orders\",\"description\":\"Perps WebSocket order placement.\",\"asyncapi\":\"asyncapi-perps.json placeOrders\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/wss/perps-place-orders\"},{\"title\":\"Modify Orders\",\"description\":\"Perps WebSocket order modification by order ID.\",\"asyncapi\":\"asyncapi-perps.json modifyOrders\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/wss/perps-modify-orders\"},{\"title\":\"Modify Orders by Client Order ID\",\"description\":\"Perps WebSocket order modification by client order ID.\",\"asyncapi\":\"asyncapi-perps.json modifyOrdersCOID\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/wss/perps-modify-orders-coid\"},{\"title\":\"Cancel Orders\",\"description\":\"Perps WebSocket order cancellation by order ID.\",\"asyncapi\":\"asyncapi-perps.json cancelOrders\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/wss/perps-cancel-orders\"},{\"title\":\"Cancel Orders by Client Order ID\",\"description\":\"Perps WebSocket order cancellation by client order ID.\",\"asyncapi\":\"asyncapi-perps.json cancelOrdersCOID\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/wss/perps-cancel-orders-coid\"},{\"title\":\"Cancel All Orders\",\"description\":\"Perps WebSocket cancellation of all open orders.\",\"asyncapi\":\"asyncapi-perps.json cancelAll\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/wss/perps-cancel-all\"},{\"title\":\"Auto Cancel\",\"description\":\"Perps WebSocket dead man's switch updates.\",\"asyncapi\":\"asyncapi-perps.json autoCancel\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/wss/perps-auto-cancel\"},{\"title\":\"Update Leverage\",\"description\":\"Perps WebSocket leverage updates.\",\"asyncapi\":\"asyncapi-perps.json updateLeverage\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/wss/perps-update-leverage\"},{\"title\":\"Update Leverages\",\"description\":\"Perps WebSocket batch leverage updates.\",\"asyncapi\":\"asyncapi-perps.json updateLeverages\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/wss/perps-update-leverages\"},{\"title\":\"Update Isolated Margin\",\"description\":\"Add or remove margin from an isolated Perps position over WebSocket.\",\"asyncapi\":\"asyncapi-perps.json updateMargin\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/wss/perps-update-margin\"},{\"title\":\"Auth\",\"description\":\"Perps WebSocket authentication.\",\"asyncapi\":\"asyncapi-perps.json auth\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/wss/perps-auth\"},{\"title\":\"Trades\",\"description\":\"Perps WebSocket public trade updates.\",\"asyncapi\":\"asyncapi-perps.json trades\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/wss/perps-trades\"},{\"title\":\"BBO\",\"description\":\"Perps WebSocket best bid and offer updates.\",\"asyncapi\":\"asyncapi-perps.json bbo\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/wss/perps-bbo\"},{\"title\":\"Book\",\"description\":\"Perps WebSocket order book updates.\",\"asyncapi\":\"asyncapi-perps.json book\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/wss/perps-book\"},{\"title\":\"Klines\",\"description\":\"Perps WebSocket candle updates.\",\"asyncapi\":\"asyncapi-perps.json klines\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/wss/perps-klines\"},{\"title\":\"Tickers\",\"description\":\"Perps WebSocket ticker updates.\",\"asyncapi\":\"asyncapi-perps.json tickers\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/wss/perps-tickers\"},{\"title\":\"Statistics\",\"description\":\"Perps WebSocket 24-hour statistics updates.\",\"asyncapi\":\"asyncapi-perps.json statistics\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/wss/perps-statistics\"},{\"title\":\"Fills\",\"description\":\"Perps WebSocket private fill updates.\",\"asyncapi\":\"asyncapi-perps.json fills\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/wss/perps-fills\"},{\"title\":\"Orders\",\"description\":\"Perps WebSocket private order updates.\",\"asyncapi\":\"asyncapi-perps.json orders\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/wss/perps-orders\"},{\"title\":\"Funding\",\"description\":\"Perps WebSocket private funding updates.\",\"asyncapi\":\"asyncapi-perps.json funding\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/wss/perps-funding\"},{\"title\":\"Balances\",\"description\":\"Perps WebSocket private balance updates.\",\"asyncapi\":\"asyncapi-perps.json balances\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/wss/perps-balances\"},{\"title\":\"Portfolio\",\"description\":\"Perps WebSocket private portfolio updates.\",\"asyncap